{"title":"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The probability of U2 dismantling an atomic bomb is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/7/5c721d9185d8cee161c314daa47431048be9b095.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. The probability of Coldplay finding X &amp; Y is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/c/f3c3a6f75914b4990d3e217a08287fc53ea31ef3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" />. If the probability of both events occurring is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/0/620f9d8ae5a5f5d63ec197c37d4cbd8cf5575d20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6\\%,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"19\" /> find the probability that neither occurs.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the Principle of Inclusion-Exclusion, the probability of U2 dismantling an atomic bomb and Coldplay NOT finding X &amp; Y is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/0/2a0b4308bf7ce96ef1da8e0479da9c579794962c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11\\%-6\\%=5\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"17\" />. Similarly, the probability of Coldplay finding X &amp; Y and U2 NOT dismantling an atomic bomb is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/a/eea484a851af22603238ef5b83067faf8f4c51b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" />. Therefore, the probability that neither occurs is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/d/5ddb253c229c791e5c20aa451ce27d5a02398d54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100\\%-5\\%-17\\%-6\\%=\\boxed{72\\%}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"262\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest\" title=\"2005 iTest\">2005 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems\">(Problems</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2005 iTest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\